  "notes": "Compound of {身|み} (body) + {震|ふる}い (shaking), with rendaku changing ふ to ぶ. Functions as both a noun and a する verb.\n\nUnlike {震|ふる}える (to tremble), which describes sustained shaking, {身震|みぶる}い typically refers to a sudden, involuntary shudder — a brief whole-body reaction.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {身震|みぶる}いする (to shudder)\n- {身震|みぶる}いがする (to feel a shudder)\n- {身震|みぶる}いするほど (enough to make one shudder)\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}で{身震|みぶる}いする (to shudder with fear)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {震|ふる}える: to tremble, to shake (sustained trembling)\n- {鳥肌|とりはだ}: goosebumps (a related physical reaction)\n- {武者震|むしゃぶる}い: trembling with excitement before action (anticipatory)",
